.TH "ROBNE" "1" "Oct 2026" "ros-ocp-backend devel" "robne CLI"

.SH NAME
robne-explain - Show explanation factors for one recommendation


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrobne explain [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Re-run the engine from the same --input as recommend and print why one
recommendation is that number.

.PP
recommend JSON is the list (what to apply) and does not include explanation
factors. explain is the detail. It does not read a recommend envelope.

.PP
One entity type per run. --plugins is exactly one name (omit for container).
Two or more names is an error. YAML plugins: does not select the type.

.PP
Identity flags (inapplicable flags are errors):
  container (default): --namespace --workload --container --term --engine
  namespace:           --namespace --term --engine
  node:                --node --term --engine
  gpu MIG:             --container plus --namespace --workload --term
  gpu timeslicing:     --node --gpu-model --term
  pvc:                 --namespace --pvc --term
  vm:                  --namespace --vm-name --term --engine
  quota:               --namespace --quota-name
  cluster-quota:    --cluster-quota-name
  snapshot:            --namespace --snapshot-name
  hcp:                 --scenario (one of request, low_qps, average_qps,
                       medium_qps, high_qps) plus optional --observed-at
                       (RFC3339; default latest)

.PP
GPU: --container selects MIG; --node without --container selects timeslicing.
--schedule business_hours is container, namespace, node, gpu, and vm
(not pvc / quota / cluster-quota / snapshot / hcp).


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--cluster-quota-name\fP=""
	ClusterResourceQuota name

.PP
\fB--config\fP=""
	YAML overlay (skips ./robne.yaml; still overlays the user file)

.PP
\fB--container\fP=""
	container name (container explain; GPU MIG)

.PP
\fB--engine\fP=""
	engine (cost, performance)

.PP
\fB--gpu-model\fP=""
	GPU model name

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for explain

.PP
\fB--input\fP=[]
	directory, .csv, .tar.gz, or postgres:// URL (recompute from stored digests); repeatable — the first payload is the primary (recommendation cluster), later payloads are advisory context (e.g. the HCP management cluster's topology)

.PP
\fB--namespace\fP=""
	namespace

.PP
\fB--no-user-config\fP[=false]
	skip user YAML/JSON (same as ROBNE_NO_USER_CONFIG=1)

.PP
\fB--node\fP=""
	node name (node explain; GPU timeslicing)

.PP
\fB--now\fP=""
	RFC3339 decay/staleness clock (does not slide term windows; default is max interval_end)

.PP
\fB--observed-at\fP=""
	hcp capacity observation timestamp (RFC3339; default latest)

.PP
\fB--pg-url-file\fP=""
	file containing a postgres URL (password off argv)

.PP
\fB--plugins\fP=""
	exactly one entity type (default: container). YAML plugins: does not select the type

.PP
\fB--pvc\fP=""
	PVC name

.PP
\fB--quota-name\fP=""
	namespace ResourceQuota name

.PP
\fB--rate-card\fP=""
	rate-card JSON overlay (skips ./rate-card.json)

.PP
\fB--recommendation-type\fP=""
	quota / cluster-quota recommendation type when the match is not unique

.PP
\fB--scenario\fP=""
	hcp capacity scenario (request, low_qps, average_qps, medium_qps, high_qps)

.PP
\fB--schedule\fP=""
	all_hours (default) or business_hours (container, namespace, node, gpu, vm)

.PP
\fB--snapshot-name\fP=""
	VolumeSnapshot name

.PP
\fB--term\fP=""
	term (short, medium, long; VM uses short_term / medium_term / long_term)

.PP
\fB--vm-name\fP=""
	VM name

.PP
\fB--workload\fP=""
	workload name

.PP
\fB--workload-type\fP=""
	workload type (required when the container match is not unique)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrobne(1)\fP


